// assets/catalog/media_style.ron
// House style and prompt rules for generated unit and structure media (Veo clips).
//
// `asset_baker` alone reads this file; the simulation and the client never do. A Veo prompt is
// composed as: the identity's authored `veo_prompts[State]` (units.ron, structures.ron), then
// the action text below for that state and the identity's drawing kind (`unit_sphere` or
// `building_dome`, or the identity's override), then the style sentence. A clip's negative
// prompt is the global one of `media/veo_request.ron` plus its kind's `negative_terms`.
// Editing this file changes every future prompt and needs no rebuild (charter §3.3). Clips
// that already exist are not regenerated for a change here.
//
// The rules below are checked by `asset_baker validate-prompts`, and by `generate-veo` before it
// reads any credential, for every clip a run would pay for.
(
    // Ends every prompt. It describes the look in plain words and names no game, studio, show
    // or franchise (see `deny_list`). It avoids "cinematic", "hero framing" and "portrait",
    // which invited camera moves, and asks for a plain backdrop: "radial studio backdrop" gave
    // radiating stripes, which the owner rejected (2026-11-04).
    style: "Stylized hand-painted 3D character, painterly sci-fi aesthetic with crisp rim lighting, plain flat uniform dark slate-indigo studio backdrop (#0B101B) with no pattern, no rays, no stripes and no gradient, 3/4 isometric front view, glowing cyan/amber energy cores, bold proportions.",

    // Action text per drawing kind, placed between the identity's prompt and the style
    // (docs/plans/2026-11-04-veo-structure-action-text.md, D-1 and D-2). It mirrors `framing`:
    // `unit_sphere` for mobile units, `building_dome` for structures, then per-identity
    // overrides. Every state an identity publishes needs a text for its kind or an override,
    // and every text is checked like a prompt (deny list, placeholder markers).
    // - texts: one text per animation state.
    // - negative_terms: plain nouns appended, after ", ", to the global `negative_prompt` of
    //   `media/veo_request.ron` for every clip of the kind. `None` adds nothing.
    actions: (
        // Mobile units. A golden list of the unit prompts' SHA-256 guards these texts. Idle and
        // Walk loop in the game, so they ask for a fixed camera and an end pose equal to the
        // start pose (owner, Q0026: jumps when a loop restarts are distracting). Constructing is
        // kept in case a unit ever publishes it; it shows work in progress on the finished shape
        // (keyframe chaining).
        // Cast (reviewed in batch 4, 2026-11-05): the atlas loops Cast and the policy pins both
        // ends, so the text now has the camera and loop clauses Idle and Walk have, and the
        // body and tools hold still. The earlier "tool arms reaching toward a target" moved the
        // pose away from the picture the clip must return to (batch 2, welder_drone, whose
        // override this text now follows). A Cast whose effect is steady (a beam, an arc)
        // still needs its own pin with the effect lit (batch-2 evidence).
        unit_sphere: (
            texts: {
                Constructing: "Constructing animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans. Construction work in progress over the whole structure, holographic wireframe scaffolding shimmering around it with active seam welding sparks. The structure keeps its shape, size and place in frame, and the last frame matches the first.",
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the subject keeps the same size and place in frame from start to end. Steady rhythmic breathing movement, subtle weapon glow pulse, head and radar scanning smoothly in place. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the subject moves in place, keeping the same size and place in frame. Dynamic forward stride, rhythmic mechanical bobbing, ground dust kick-up at feet, leaning into movement. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation: sharp weapon recoil, intense bright muzzle flash and projectile emission filling the right side of frame, followed by fluid spring recovery.",
                Cast: "Cast animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the subject keeps the same size, pose and place in frame from start to end. It holds a steady bright work beam or extraction arc toward a point just outside the frame, with showering sparks, its body and tools holding still. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Die: "Death animation: dramatic armor fracture, glowing internal reactor blowout with flying mechanical debris dissolving into smoke.",
            },
            // "Breathing" is asked for above, so it cannot be a negative term for units.
            negative_terms: None,
        ),
        // Structures. Idle is a completely still building: fixed geometry, small ambient
        // effects only, no moving parts, no breathing or pulsing of the shape, and a locked
        // camera. The unit Idle text ("breathing", "radar scanning", "glow pulse") gave a
        // breathing camera and a changing antenna on the siphon pilot (batch-1 evidence).
        // Constructing shows the build-up on the finished shape with no camera motion, and its
        // effects fade so that its last frame equals the clean Idle pin (loops plan D-3).
        building_dome: (
            texts: {
                Constructing: "Constructing animation, one locked-off static shot: the camera never moves, zooms or drifts. The finished building keeps its final shape, size and place in frame throughout while construction plays over it: holographic wireframe scaffolding shimmering around it and welding sparks along its seams, fading away toward the end. The last frame matches the first.",
                Idle: "Idle animation, one locked-off static shot: the camera never moves, zooms or drifts. A completely still building, fixed rigid geometry, no moving parts: shell, roof, antenna and pipes keep the same shape, size and place throughout. Only small ambient effects move: a steady glow, gentle vapour rising, small lights flickering. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
            },
            // Not in the global list: units ask for breathing. "Flickering geometry" is left
            // out, because a negative "flickering" may suppress the lights Idle asks for.
            negative_terms: Some("breathing motion, pulsing size, swelling, shrinking, moving parts, rotating parts, antenna changing shape"),
        ),
        // Exact catalog slug -> state -> text, for one identity whose clip needs other wording.
        // An override keeps its kind's negative terms. A slug that is not in the catalog, or a
        // state the identity does not publish, is refused.
        //
        // repair_shuttle (batch 1, 2026-11-04): an unarmed aircraft. The unit Idle text asks for
        // a weapon glow and a scanning head, and the unit Walk text for a stride and dust at the
        // feet, none of which it has. Both of its looping states start and end on its hovering
        // Idle pin, so they keep that pose and show motion through the thrusters.
        //
        // welder_drone (batch 2, 2026-11-04): a hovering worker armed with a melee welding torch.
        // The unit Idle text asks for a weapon glow and a scanning head (a turning part), the
        // unit Walk text for a stride and dust at the feet, and the unit Attack text for a muzzle
        // flash and a projectile; it has none of these. The unit Cast text has no camera clause
        // and no loop clause although the atlas loops Cast and the policy pins its end, and its
        // "tool arms reaching" moves the pose away from the pin it must return to. Idle, Walk and
        // Cast start and end on the hovering Idle pin, so they keep that pose; Attack starts on it.
        //
        // railgun_crawler, shock_golem, jet_jumper, specter_android (batch 3, 2026-11-05): the
        // barracks' combat units. The unit Idle text asks for "head and radar scanning", a
        // turning part that batch 1 saw flicker and change shape; the unit Walk text asks for
        // "ground dust kick-up at feet", and words about the ground drew a floor plane in
        // batch 2; the unit Attack text has no camera clause and ends nowhere in particular.
        // Their Idle and Walk start and end on the Idle pin and Attack starts on it, so each
        // text keeps the pose, faces the weapons one way and returns to the start. The
        // crawler is a tracked tank: no feet, a fixed turret, the tracks show the travel.
        // Batch 4 (2026-11-05) redesigned it from text with no side vents (its first pin's
        // side exhaust flames flickered in five Walks) and asked its Walk for tracks running
        // fast on a rolling road with exhaust streaming backward; the golem's Walk asks for a
        // brisk march with high knee lifts (marking time read as a weight shift).
        //
        // napalm_wheeler, colossus_mech, vector_interceptor, sky_bastion, cloak_gunship,
        // omni_probe_drone (batch 5, 2026-11-06): the late units. Their authored texts named
        // turning parts ("spinning radar arrays", "rotating lift rings", "ducted fan rotors"),
        // the ground ("gravel plumes", "crushing terrain") or a change of shape (a siege anchor,
        // a missile salvo after the cannons), and were rewritten. The trike follows the
        // crawler (fixed parts at rest, wheels running on a rolling road), the mech the golem
        // (a still Idle, a brisk march on the spot, fire and settle back), and the four
        // aircraft the shuttle (hover with a bob, fly in place, no ground contact), with an
        // Attack that fires forward and returns to the hover pose.
        // The trike and the mech were re-seeded from text in batch 5b (2026-11-09): the trike's
        // first pin had fine painterly detail and a cyan outline glow that shimmered in ten
        // Idles, and its wheels never turned in three Walks, so it asks for bold clean plates,
        // no outline glow and spoked hubs that show the wheels turning; the mech's held-out
        // arm-cannons shifted in nine Idles, so its arms hang low, its Idle stands completely
        // still (as the aircraft's), its Walk names "never leans or steps toward the camera"
        // first, and its Attack raises the cannons, fires and lowers them again.
        // burrow_scorpion (batch 6, 2026-11-09): the Lurker analogue, the first creature of the
        // Sylvan Swarm with generated media. Its authored texts named the ground ("digging into
        // loose soil", "parting dust", "erupting from ground"), which drew floor planes in
        // batches 2 and 5, and were rewritten as a whole beast seen at 3/4 with no floor. It
        // follows the golem's pattern: a still crouch, a crawl on the spot that never turns
        // toward the camera, and an Attack that strikes and settles back to the Idle pose.
        // Its first pin (spread claws, raised legs) failed five Idles and five Walks, so it was
        // re-seeded in a compact crouch; on that pin the Idle reads "as still as a statue", the
        // Walk names legs that "clearly lift and step", and Walk and Attack ask for the smooth
        // backdrop to stay unchanged (two clips turned it into grainy sand).
        // The client shows no burrowed form (the burrowed mode is drawn cloaked on the same
        // atlas), so the atlas holds the three published states only.
        // mothership_carrier, saucer_interceptor (carrier batch, 2026-11-26; plan
        // 2026-11-28-carrier-interceptors WP5): the Carrier and the interceptors it launches, the
        // first Cosmic Enclave aircraft with generated media. Their authored texts named a
        // cloudscape (a scene), a "massive shadow" (a floor to cast it on), "spinning rim lights"
        // (a turning part) and "a fast banking glide" and "a strafing pass" (travel and a turn),
        // and were rewritten on the aircraft pattern of batch 5: a still hover, flight in place
        // shown by light and vapour trails (a saucer has no exhaust), and an Attack that fires
        // or launches forward and returns to the hover pose. The interceptor's beams and the
        // Carrier's drones leave toward the lower right, the way both face.
        // Their Idle texts (the seed pictures) were reworded in the continuation under Q0131 on the
        // Brood Lord analogue's pattern: "seen from above … looking down on its top", a plain dark
        // backdrop, no "high above" or "floating"; the Carrier's first seed on it had no shafts.
        // spore_matriarch, brood_mite (broodlings batch, 2026-11-26; plan 2026-11-28-broodlings
        // WP6, D-12): the Brood Lord analogue and the Broodling it throws, the second and third
        // Sylvan Swarm creatures with generated media. The Brood Lord analogue is described as a
        // creature, not an aircraft (the Carrier's saucers drew light shafts, Q0131), with no sky,
        // cloud, "high above", "hovering" or lit-from-above wording: a still pose with its wings
        // spread, a glide in place with rippling wings, and an Attack that flings two larvae
        // toward the lower right. The Broodling follows the scorpion's pattern: a still crouch,
        // a scuttle on a treadmill, and a stab that settles back to the Idle pose.
        overrides: {
            "spore_matriarch": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the beast keeps the same size and place in frame. It holds still, wings spread: it never turns, tilts or bobs; only its amber spore pods pulse softly. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the beast glides forward in place, as if held in a wind tunnel, keeping the same size, place and three-quarter facing in frame: its broad wings ripple in slow even waves from the first frame to the last. The plain dark backdrop stays unchanged. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the beast keeps its place in frame. It flings two small wriggling pale larvae from under its belly straight toward the lower right and out of the frame, then holds still in its starting pose. The plain dark backdrop stays unchanged throughout.",
            },
            "brood_mite": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the larva keeps the same size, pose and place in frame. It crouches as still as a statue: its body, head, legs and claws never move, turn or nod; its colours and light never change. The plain dark backdrop stays unchanged. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans. The larva scuttles on a treadmill that holds it in place: its short hooked legs clearly lift and step in quick turns at an even pace from the first frame to the last, while its body and claws stay at exactly the same place, size and three-quarter facing in frame; it never moves forward, back or toward the camera. The plain dark backdrop stays unchanged. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the larva keeps its place in frame. It rears and stabs forward twice with its two curved needle claws toward the lower right, then settles smoothly back to its starting pose. The plain dark backdrop stays unchanged throughout.",
            },
            "mothership_carrier": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the carrier keeps the same size and place in frame. The carrier hangs still in the air: it never turns, tilts or bobs, and only its rim bays and central core glow and blink softly. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the carrier flies forward in place, as if held in a wind tunnel, keeping the same size, pose and place in frame. From the first frame to the last its rim bays glow bright and long thin vapour trails stream back from its rim toward the upper left, flickering at an even pace; no ground contact. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the carrier keeps its place in frame, hovering. The docking bays on its front rim flash open and a quick stream of tiny golden saucer drones flies out of them, one after another, straight toward the lower right and out of the frame, then the bays dim and the carrier hovers in its starting pose.",
            },
            "saucer_interceptor": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the drone keeps the same size and place in frame. The drone hangs still in the air: it never turns, tilts or bobs, and only its amber core and small rim lights glow and blink softly. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the drone flies at full speed in place, as if held in a wind tunnel, keeping the same size, pose and place in frame. From the first frame to the last its rim lights blaze and long thin bright light trails stream back from its rim toward the upper left, flickering at an even pace; no ground contact. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the drone keeps its place in frame, hovering. It fires forward: two short bright amber energy beams flash from the front of its rim straight toward the lower right and out of the frame, then the beams fade and it hovers in its starting pose.",
            },
            "burrow_scorpion": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the scorpion keeps the same size, pose and place in frame. It crouches as still as a statue: body, legs, claws and tail never move; only the amber bands on its back glow steadily. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans. The scorpion scuttles on a treadmill that holds it in place: its six legs clearly lift and step in quick turns at an even pace from the first frame to the last, while its body, claws and tail stay at exactly the same place, size and three-quarter facing in frame; it never moves forward, back or toward the camera. The smooth plain backdrop stays unchanged. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the scorpion keeps its place in frame. It hunches and drives its spined tail down: a straight row of jagged bone spikes bursts up in a quick ripple in front of it toward the right edge of the frame, then the spikes sink away and it rises smoothly back to its starting pose. The smooth plain backdrop stays unchanged throughout.",
            },
            "napalm_wheeler": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the trike keeps the same size and place in frame from start to end. The trike is parked and switched off: it never moves, rocks or turns, its wheels are locked still with steady hub lights, the barrel stays fixed; no smoke, no fire. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the trike drives at full speed on a rolling road that holds it in place: all three wheels spin fast and continuously from the first frame to the last, their bright spoked hubs and tread blocks clearly turning around the axles, while the hull keeps the same place, size and facing in frame. The hull rides steady and level and the barrel stays fixed and dark; the plain backdrop stays empty and still. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the trike keeps its place in frame. Its front barrel shoots a short roaring jet of fire straight forward along its line and out of the frame, then the flame dies away and the trike settles back to its starting position.",
            },
            "colossus_mech": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the subject keeps the same size, pose and place in frame from start to end. The mech stands still holding its fire, keeping its three-quarter view: it never turns toward the camera, sways or shifts, arms hanging low and fixed; only its small lights glow steadily. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the mech never turns, leans or steps toward the camera: its chest and feet keep facing the lower right of the frame, at the same place and size, from the first frame to the last. It marks time on the spot without travelling: short heavy steps, left, right, left, right, each foot lifting a little and stamping back down in the same footprint at an even pace, both arm-cannons hanging low at its sides. Nothing else appears in the frame. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the subject keeps its place in frame. It raises both arm-cannons level and fires them forward: a heavy recoil, bright muzzle flashes and shells streaking out of frame, then it lowers both arms smoothly back to its starting pose.",
            },
            "vector_interceptor": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the aircraft keeps the same size and place in frame from start to end. The aircraft hangs still in the air: it never turns, tilts or bobs, and only its engines and small wing lights glow and blink softly. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the aircraft flies at full speed in place, as if held in a wind tunnel, keeping the same size, pose and place in frame. From the first frame to the last its engines blaze with long bright exhaust flames streaming backward, flickering at an even pace, and thin vapour trails stream back from its wingtips; no ground contact. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the aircraft keeps its place in frame, hovering. It fires forward along its nose: a bright launch flash at the pods and two torpedoes streaking straight out of the frame, then the smoke clears and it hovers in its starting pose.",
            },
            "sky_bastion": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the aircraft keeps the same size and place in frame from start to end. The aircraft hangs still in the air: it never turns, tilts or bobs, and only its two fixed lift rings and small hull lights glow and blink softly. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the aircraft flies at full speed in place, as if held in a wind tunnel, keeping the same size, pose and place in frame. From the first frame to the last its engines blaze with long bright exhaust flames streaming backward, flickering at an even pace, and thin vapour trails stream back from its wingtips; no ground contact. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the aircraft keeps its place in frame, hovering. It fires forward along its nose: a bright launch flash at the pods and two rockets streaking straight out of the frame, then the smoke clears and it hovers in its starting pose.",
            },
            "cloak_gunship": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the aircraft keeps the same size and place in frame from start to end. The aircraft hovers in place with a gentle steady bob, its nacelle vents glowing softly and small hull lights blinking; its body and every part keep the same shape and facing. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the aircraft flies at full speed in place, as if held in a wind tunnel, keeping the same size, pose and place in frame. From the first frame to the last its two engine nacelles glow bright orange and long exhaust flames and vapour trails stream out behind them toward the upper left of the frame, flickering at an even pace; no ground contact. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the aircraft keeps its place in frame, hovering. It fires forward along its nose: a bright launch flash at the pods and a quick salvo of orange rockets streaking straight out of the frame, then the smoke clears and it hovers in its starting pose.",
            },
            "omni_probe_drone": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the drone keeps the same size and place in frame from start to end. The drone hangs still in the air: it never turns, tilts or bobs, its arms and fins stay fixed, and only its sensor lenses and small lights glow and blink softly. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the drone flies in place, keeping the same size, pose and place in frame. Its small thrusters flare in steady bursts, exhaust streams backward, a slight rhythmic bob, no ground contact. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
            },
            "railgun_crawler": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the tank keeps the same size and place in frame from start to end. The tank sits still with its engine idling: thin exhaust smoke drifts slowly from its two rear stacks and blue energy glows steadily along the rails. The turret, both barrels and the tracks stay fixed. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the tank drives at full speed on a rolling road that holds it in place: all four tracks run fast and continuously, treads and road wheels visibly moving the whole time, while the hull keeps the same place, size and facing in frame. The hull vibrates on its suspension and exhaust smoke streams backward from its two rear stacks; the turret stays fixed. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the tank keeps its place in frame with the turret fixed. The twin rails fire once along the barrels: a sharp recoil, a bright blue electric flash at the muzzles and a bolt streaking out of frame, then the barrels settle back to their starting position.",
            },
            "shock_golem": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the subject keeps the same size, pose and place in frame from start to end. It stands still and steady in place, holding its fire: its body barely moves and only its lights change, optics glowing and energy cores pulsing softly; head and weapons keep facing the same way. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans. The golem marches briskly on the spot as if on a treadmill: four full steps, left, right, left, right, each knee lifting high and each foot stamping down again at an even pace from the first frame to the last, while its body keeps the same place, size and three-quarter facing in frame and never leans toward the camera. Weapons held ready; nothing else appears in the frame. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the subject keeps its place in frame. It fires along the line its weapons point: a sharp recoil, bright muzzle flashes and shells streaking out of frame, then it settles smoothly back to its starting pose.",
            },
            "jet_jumper": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the subject keeps the same size, pose and place in frame from start to end. It stands still and steady in place, holding its fire: its body barely moves and only its lights change, optics glowing and energy cores pulsing softly; head and weapons keep facing the same way. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the subject runs on the spot as if on a treadmill: its legs step in turn while its body keeps the same place, size and three-quarter facing in frame throughout. A steady rhythmic stride with a slight mechanical bob, weapons held ready. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the subject keeps its place in frame. It fires along the line its weapons point: a sharp recoil, bright muzzle flashes and projectiles streaking out of frame, then it settles smoothly back to its starting pose.",
            },
            "specter_android": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the subject keeps the same size, pose and place in frame from start to end. It stands still and steady in place, holding its fire: its body barely moves and only its lights change, optics glowing and energy cores pulsing softly; head and rifle keep facing the same way. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the subject marches on the spot as if on a treadmill: its legs step in turn while its body keeps the same place, size and three-quarter facing in frame throughout. A steady rhythmic stride with a slight mechanical bob, rifle held ready. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the subject keeps its place in frame. It fires once along the line its rifle points: a sharp recoil, a bright muzzle flash and a beam streaking out of frame, then it settles smoothly back to its starting pose.",
            },
            "welder_drone": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the subject keeps the same size and place in frame from start to end. The robot hovers in place with a gentle steady bob, its optic eye glowing, a small blue pilot flame flickering at the welding torch tip. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the robot flies in place, keeping the same size, pose and place in frame. Its back thrusters flare in steady bursts, exhaust streams backward, a slight rhythmic bob, no ground contact. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the robot keeps its place in frame. A quick close-range jab of its welding torch arm toward the right side of the frame, a burst of bright orange sparks at the tool tip, then the arm swings back to its starting pose.",
                Cast: "Cast animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the robot hovers in place keeping the same size, pose and place in frame. Its welding torch holds a steady bright welding arc toward a point just outside the frame, with showering sparks, and its claw glows softly. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
