            "repair_shuttle": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the subject keeps the same size and place in frame from start to end. The aircraft hovers in place with a gentle steady bob, thrusters glowing, nanite emitters shimmering softly. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the aircraft flies in place, keeping the same size, pose and place in frame. Thrusters flare in steady bursts, exhaust streams backward, a slight rhythmic bob, no ground contact. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
            },
        // Batch 2 for an outside generator (docs/media/veo-video-requests-batch-2.md, 2026-11-28):
        // the 24 Cosmic Enclave and Sylvan Swarm units without media. Their authored texts named
        // turning parts ("rotating crystalline rings", "spinning" glaives and prongs), the ground
        // ("over terrain", "uneven ground", "across the battlefield"), scenery ("cloud cover",
        // "airspace", "breeze"), travel and turns ("banking", "sprint leaping", "tumbling") and a
        // see-through body ("Transparent", "Shimmering translucent"), and were rewritten on the
        // patterns earlier batches proved: aircraft and drones as the Carrier (a still hover seen
        // from above, flight in place shown by light trails toward the upper left, fire toward
        // the lower right and return to the hover); winged creatures as the Brood Lord analogue
        // (still wings, a glide in place with rippling wings); ground creatures as the scorpion
        // and the Broodling (a still crouch, a scuttle on a treadmill, a strike that settles
        // back); the Greys and the walkers as the golem and the mech (stand still, march on the
        // spot, fire and settle back). Enclave units are silver and gold with violet and cyan
        // lights; Swarm units are dark green and brown chitin with amber glow.
            "flying_saucer": {
                Idle: "Idle animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the saucer keeps the same size and place in frame. The saucer hangs still in the air: it never turns, tilts or bobs, and only its violet rim lights and emitter lens glow and blink softly. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Walk: "Walk animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the saucer flies forward in place, as if held in a wind tunnel, keeping the same size, pose and place in frame. From the first frame to the last its rim lights blaze and long thin violet light trails stream back from it toward the upper left, flickering at an even pace; no ground contact. Seamless loop: the last frame matches the first.",
                Attack: "Attack animation, one static tripod shot: the camera never moves, zooms or pans, and the saucer keeps its place in frame, hovering. A thin steady violet beam streams from the emitter at its front edge straight toward the lower right and out of the frame, then the beam fades and it hovers in its starting pose.",
            },
